course: dictionary
lesson: 2227
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and covered is one of them. To find the right meaning, look at the words around it. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence.
explain: «Many Indus houses had bathrooms and toilets connected to covered drains along the streets.» Covered means having something over it, so these drains had a cover over them. Try your meaning in the sentence: the drains had a cover over them, and that makes sense.
explain: Covered can also mean having a lot of something all over. «A snow leopard's wide, fur-covered paws» means its paws have fur all over them. In maths, covered can mean distance travelled: «covered 30 miles» means someone travelled 30 miles.
explain: Covered is also the past of cover. Cover, covers, covering and covered all come from the same verb. When you meet covered, check the words around it before you decide which meaning it has.
fact: Covered means having something over it or on it.
fact: Covered is the past of cover: cover, covers, covering, covered.
fact: «Covered in» means having a lot of something all over, like «covered in mud».
fact: In maths, «covered 30 miles» means the distance already travelled.
fact: In science, most of Earth is covered by water.
exercise: «Many Indus houses had bathrooms connected to covered drains.» What does covered mean here? | Painted in bright colours | Full of people | *Having a cover over them | Very wide and very deep
exercise: «The runner covered 30 miles before lunch.» What does covered mean here? | Had mud all over | *Travelled over a distance | Hidden under a sheet | Lost the race
exercise: «A snow leopard's fur-covered paws spread its weight like snowshoes.» What does fur-covered mean? | Shaped like a snowshoe | Made of fur only at the tips | *Having fur all over | Lost all of its fur
test: «Antarctica is ice-covered land.» What does ice-covered mean? | *Having ice all over | Melting into water | Lost in a storm | Very hot and dry
test: Which word is the past of cover? | *covered | covering | covers | coverer
exam: «A covered bridge» is a bridge that is | Only used by boats | Very long and narrow | *Roofed, with something over it | Made of ice
